<Layout title="Suppliers — Bangalore packaging procurement for MGS" description="Research-backed supplier shortlist for glass jars, caps, induction foil, EPE liners, labels, and tamper strips — Bangalore-first, India-wide fallbacks. The honest map of who does what.">
  <main class="bg-cream min-h-screen">
    <!-- HERO -->
    <header class="border-b border-ink/10">
      <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 py-16">
        <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-spice-500 font-medium mb-4">Procurement research · Bangalore + India</p>
        <h1 class="font-serif text-4xl md:text-5xl text-ink mb-5 leading-tight">Packaging suppliers<br/>— who makes what, where</h1>
        <p class="text-ink/70 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed">
          The honest answer: <strong>no single Bangalore vendor manufactures jar + cap + foil + label + cap-printing in one place</strong>. Most "Bangalore glass jar" listings are TRADERS sourcing from the actual factories (Firozabad UP, Jabalpur MP, Hyderabad). The realistic shortlist is <strong>3 suppliers across 5 components</strong> — plus a co-packing alternative that skips manufacturing entirely.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-5 text-sm">
          <a href="/plan" class="text-spice underline hover:text-spice-700">← Back to the launch plan</a>
          <span class="text-ink/40 mx-2">·</span>
          <a href="/setup" class="text-spice underline hover:text-spice-700">Setup checklist</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- REALITY CHECK -->
    <section class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 py-12 border-b border-ink/10">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl text-ink mb-2">1. The "one-stop shop" reality</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink/60 mb-6">Tested against IndiaMART + TradeIndia + Justdial + ExportersIndia listings, May 2026.</p>

      <p class="sup-body">
        Indian packaging is <strong>fragmented by component</strong>:
      </p>
      <ul class="sup-bullets">
        <li><strong>Glass jars</strong> are physically made in <strong>Firozabad (UP)</strong> — India's dominant cluster, ~80% of glass containers — plus <strong>Hyderabad / Bhongir (Telangana)</strong> via AGI Glaspac and <strong>Indore (MP)</strong> via Mahalaxmi Industries. Note: <strong>Jabalpur is NOT a glass-jar hub</strong> despite some online listings — it's primarily plastic + general packaging. Bangalore "manufacturers" are usually traders/distributors who place orders with the actual Firozabad/Hyderabad/Indore factories.</li>
        <li><strong>Metal caps</strong> are made by specialised closure companies — different supply chain from glass.</li>
        <li><strong>Induction foils</strong> + EPE liners come from foil/wad specialists (different again).</li>
        <li><strong>Labels</strong> come from local print shops.</li>
        <li><strong>Cap printing</strong> (foil stamping / pad print) is usually done by the cap manufacturer OR a specialty printer.</li>
      </ul>

      <p class="sup-body" style="margin-top: 16px;">
        The closest thing to "one-stop" is using a <strong>trader-distributor like Amigo Sampoorna (Bangalore) or Ajanta Bottle (Delhi-shipped)</strong> who buy from the factories and pass on to you with their margin. Convenient but not cheap.
      </p>

      <div class="sup-callout">
        <p class="sup-callout-label">The realistic 3-supplier model</p>
        <p>For 500–1,000 jar pilot scale, plan on contracting with:</p>
        <ol class="sup-step-list" style="margin-top: 10px;">
          <li><strong>Supplier A — Jar + Cap + Foil seal kit</strong> — a Bangalore trader/distributor (e.g., Amigo Sampoorna) OR a national glass house (e.g., Ajanta Bottle) who supplies jar + matching cap + induction foil from inventory</li>
          <li><strong>Supplier B — Labels</strong> — a local Bangalore print shop (e.g., Kraftix Digital, Sahara Labels) for the wraparound label, low MOQ, fast turnaround</li>
          <li><strong>Supplier C — Tamper strips + cap print</strong> — a label printer for the strip, or a closure specialist (e.g., Metal Closures Pvt Ltd Bangalore) for printed caps when you scale to State License + retail</li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </section>

